{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S8EgQvmvYLPhDMtzAXoVTq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: pi-lhc-epic-01-connector-core-build\n3\tdescription: Autonomous orchestration (impl-lead) of the pi-lhc Epic 1 Connector Core build via lbuild-impl ls-impl; durable run state lives in team-impl-log.md.\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: c60a53bf-54ba-4447-8e83-5ae7d2b4edb8\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tLee tasked an autonomous, long-horizon orchestration (I am impl-lead) of the **pi-lhc Epic 1 \"Connector Core\"** build using the `lbuild-impl` CLI + `ls-impl` skill. Spec pack root: `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/` (epic.md, tech-design.md, test-plan.md, stories 00-foundation … 06-startup-validation). pi-lhc is a PI extension that hosts the LHC SDK (`packages/pi-lhc`, workspace-depends on `packages/lhc`). Epic 1 is **observe-only**: capture PI hook traffic into LHC threads, derive LHC turns from PI traffic (PI fires turn-per-step; one LHC turn = whole exchange, closed at agent_end), route derivation inference through PI's auth — change nothing the model sees.\n11\t\n12\t**Why:** Multi-story provider-backed build spanning hours; state must survive context compaction and session restarts, so it is kept on disk, not in conversation.\n13\t\n14\t**How to apply:** On resume, read `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md` FIRST (it holds State, Current Story, Current Phase, story receipts, baselines, continuation handles) plus `impl-run.config.json` and `artifacts/`, and continue from the recorded State — do NOT reconstruct from memory of prior turns. Provider config: story-lead+verifier+quick-fixer = codex/gpt-5.5, implementor = claude-opus-4-8/max (codex auth confirmed working). Story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`; epic gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all`. Stories touching `packages/lhc` (e.g. Story 1's A-8 registry additions) also need `pnpm --filter lhc verify` at acceptance since configured gates are pi-lhc-scoped. Commit per accepted story on `main` with scoped pathspecs — a large pre-existing lhc-docs reorg (~1267 entries) sits staged in the index; keep it OUT of story commits. Long provider runs: background them and watch with a ~5-min Monitor on the status.json until terminal. See [[lbuild-impl-needs-ruling-on-implementor-deviations]].\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc8b0d70-702e-4abc-9faa-dda18cc81eaf","uuid":"b33f828a-374b-4bfc-af9f-4da2331d4267","timestamp":"2026-06-14T05:23:33.645Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/.claude/projects/-Users-leemoore-code-pi-long-horizon-liminal-context/memory/pi-lhc-epic-01-connector-core-build.md","content":"---\nname: pi-lhc-epic-01-connector-core-build\ndescription: Autonomous orchestration (impl-lead) of the pi-lhc Epic 1 Connector Core build via lbuild-impl ls-impl; durable run state lives in team-impl-log.md.\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c60a53bf-54ba-4447-8e83-5ae7d2b4edb8\n---\n\nLee tasked an autonomous, long-horizon orchestration (I am impl-lead) of the **pi-lhc Epic 1 \"Connector Core\"** build using the `lbuild-impl` CLI + `ls-impl` skill. Spec pack root: `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/` (epic.md, tech-design.md, test-plan.md, stories 00-foundation … 06-startup-validation). pi-lhc is a PI extension that hosts the LHC SDK (`packages/pi-lhc`, workspace-depends on `packages/lhc`). Epic 1 is **observe-only**: capture PI hook traffic into LHC threads, derive LHC turns from PI traffic (PI fires turn-per-step; one LHC turn = whole exchange, closed at agent_end), route derivation inference through PI's auth — change nothing the model sees.\n\n**Why:** Multi-story provider-backed build spanning hours; state must survive context compaction and session restarts, so it is kept on disk, not in conversation.\n\n**How to apply:** On resume, read `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md` FIRST (it holds State, Current Story, Current Phase, story receipts, baselines, continuation handles) plus `impl-run.config.json` and `artifacts/`, and continue from the recorded State — do NOT reconstruct from memory of prior turns. Provider config: story-lead+verifier+quick-fixer = codex/gpt-5.5, implementor = claude-opus-4-8/max (codex auth confirmed working). Story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`; epic gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all`. Stories touching `packages/lhc` (e.g. Story 1's A-8 registry additions) also need `pnpm --filter lhc verify` at acceptance since configured gates are pi-lhc-scoped. Commit per accepted story on `main` with scoped pathspecs — a large pre-existing lhc-docs reorg (~1267 entries) sits staged in the index; keep it OUT of story commits. Long provider runs: background them and watch with a ~5-min Monitor on the status.json until terminal. See [[lbuild-impl-needs-ruling-on-implementor-deviations]].\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
